**Day 33: MongoDB CRUD Operations**  

**Topic:**  
Detailed explanation of MongoDB CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete) operations, including `insertOne/insertMany`, `find`, `updateOne/updateMany`, and `deleteOne`. Covers query operators and practical exercises with 20 student documents.  

**Learning Objectives:**  
• Understand MongoDB CRUD operations and their syntax.  
• Learn to insert, query, update, and delete documents efficiently.  
• Apply query operators for conditional data manipulation.  

**Activities / Deliverables:**  
• Insert 20 student documents using `insertMany`.  
• Perform queries with conditions using `find`.  
• Update and delete documents using `updateOne/updateMany` and `deleteOne`.  

**Important Concepts:**  
• Atomic operations in MongoDB.  
• Flexibility of schema-less document storage.  

**SQL Syntax / Commands:**  
• `db.collection.insertOne({field: value})`  
• `db.collection.find({condition})`  
• `db.collection.updateOne({filter}, {$set: {update}})`  
• `db.collection.deleteOne({condition})`  

**Real-world Use Cases:**  
• Managing user profiles in web applications.  
• Logging and analyzing real-time data.  

**Tools / Tech:**  
• MongoDB 7  
• MongoDB Compass  

**Summary:**  
Today covered essential MongoDB CRUD operations, including inserting, querying, updating, and deleting documents. Practical exercises reinforced understanding of conditional queries and atomic updates.  

